xnu 0425: load the QCA6490 SBL through BHI (mondrianwifi=1)

W5 reads BHI 1.2 in PBL with one segment. W6 adds the load path: `wififw`
reads /private/var/vm/amss.bin from the iOS root, maps the wired buffer page
by page through the W2 SMMU context at 0xa1000000, and writes BHI_IMGADDR,
BHI_IMGSIZE and BHI_IMGTXDB. The first attempt left bus mastering off, which
W3 clears on purpose, so the device could not read the image; W6 now sets the
PCI memory and bus-master bits before the load. It also writes BHI_INTVEC and
passes only the first 512 KiB: ath11k treats amss.bin as an SBL plus AMSS
image (`sbl_size` 512 KiB) and the SBL fetches the remainder through BHIE.
The command polls BHI_STATUS for success or error and then waits for
MHISTATUS.READY, so one boot proves the transfer and whether the SBL started.

The USB command races the WiFi worker on a cold boot: the rail votes can take
a minute, so the command waits for the BAR and, behind `mondrianwififw=1`, the
worker calls the same load as soon as W4 has mapped it. The image read retries
until the root is mounted.

Facts from mainline drivers/bus/mhi/host/boot.c, pm.c and common.h
(GPL-2.0, constants only).

